{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "CEDS",
    "description": "CEDS (Community Emissions Data System) global gridded anthropogenic emissions data loader. Provides monthly surface emission fluxes (kg m⁻² s⁻¹) at 0.5° × 0.5° global resolution for 10 species: BC, CH4, CO, CO2, N2O, NH3, NMVOC, NOx, OC, SO2.\n\nData source: CEDS-CMIP release v20250421 (CEDS-CMIP-2025-04-18), available from the ORNL ESGF THREDDS server. Files are NetCDF with dimensions (time, sector, lat, lon) and variable name {species}_em_anthro. The sector dimension has 8 entries (Agriculture, Energy, Industrial, Transportation, Residential/Commercial/Other, Solvents, Waste, International Shipping); the data_loaders emit sector-summed total anthropogenic flux.\n\nTemporal coverage: 1750–2023, monthly. Data is organized in 50-year file chunks: 1750-1799, 1800-1849, 1850-1899, 1900-1949, 1950-1999, and 2000-2023. This ESM documents the modern-era chunk (2000-2023) as the primary temporal range. For simulations outside 2000-2023, different chunk file URLs are required (see reference.notes).\n\nThe gt-p3ep (@register_symbolic interp_unsafe) blocking gap is resolved by the data_loaders §8 mechanism: the runtime handles file download, sector-summing, temporal interpolation, and spatial regridding from the native 0.5°×0.5° lat/lon grid to the model domain. Each species equation is a direct pass-through: {species}_em_anthro(t) ~ CEDS_{species}.{species}_em_anthro. No registered functions remain in the migrated component.\n\nLongitude convention: the raw CEDS NC files use [0, 360) longitude. The upstream loadslice! reorders to [−180, 180) via a permutation vector computed at FileSet construction time. This ESM documents the reordered [−180, 180) coordinate as the effective spatial extent.\n\nCoupling: lon and lat parameters are coupled to the simulation domain via param_to_var when composed into a CoupledSystem. Unlike EDGAR, CEDS has no lev parameter (surface-only flux).\n\nMigrated from EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b src/ceds.jl:313 (CEDS constructor, esm-4ega).\n\n[esm-3nc.3] Split into ten pure-I/O species loaders (ceds_<species>_loader.esm) + this regridding model per RFC pure-io-data-loaders §6/§7. Each loader is referenced as the subsystem CEDS_<species>; every species flux is regridded conservatively (cell-centered emissions).",
    "tags": [
      "earthsci_data",
      "emissions",
      "anthropogenic",
      "ceds",
      "monthly",
      "data_loader",
      "surface_flux",
      "global",
      "multi_species",
      "regridding_model"
    ],
    "created": "2026-05-30T00:00:00Z",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciData.jl contributors",
      "EarthSciModels migration (esm-4ega)"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Hoesly, R. M., Smith, S. J., Feng, L., Klimont, Z., Janssens-Maenhout, G., Pitkanen, T., Seibert, J. J., Vu, L., Andres, R. J., Bolt, R. M., Bond, T. C., Dawidowski, L., Kholod, N., Kurokawa, J., Li, M., Liu, L., Lu, Z., Moura, M. C. P., O'Rourke, P. R., and Zhang, Q. (2018). Historical (1750–2014) anthropogenic emissions of reactive gases and aerosols from the Community Emissions Data System (CEDS). Geoscientific Model Development, 11, 369–408.",
        "url": "https://doi.org/10.5194/gmd-11-369-2018"
      },
      {
        "citation": "CEDS-CMIP 2025 release (v20250421, CEDS-CMIP-2025-04-18). Available from ORNL ESGF THREDDS: https://esgf-node.ornl.gov/thredds/fileServer/user_pub_work/input4MIPs/CMIP7/CMIP/PNNL-JGCRI/CEDS-CMIP-2025-04-18/"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Source: EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/ceds.jl:1-378 (CEDSFileSet, CEDS constructor). Test: test/ceds_test.jl. Docs: docs/src/ceds.md."
      }
    ]
  },
  "data_sources": {
